---
description: Apply when changing Research, Knowledge, Evidence Vault, Files ingestion, chunking or retrieval
alwaysApply: false
---
- Keep provenance for every reusable knowledge/evidence item.
- Do not invent an expert/mastery result. If evidence is insufficient, retain a truthful incomplete state.
- Research must respect network/file policies and work locally when network is unavailable.
- Preserve idempotent ingestion where possible; unchanged files should not create duplicate knowledge.
- Separate durable Memory, bulk Knowledge and source Evidence conceptually and in retrieval behavior.
- Add parser/chunking tests when adding a document format.
- Avoid loading huge source documents into one model prompt; chunk, retrieve and synthesize iteratively.
